$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for amide coupling: To a 0°C
solution of carboxylic acid (1.0 eq or 2.0 eq) in DMF (0.15 M) was added
EDC (1.2 eq or 2.4 eq) followed by HOAt (1.2 eq or 2.4 eq). After 10 min,
amine (1.0 eq) and NMM (3.0 eq or 6.0 eq) were added. The resulting
reaction mixture was allowed to warm to room temperature overnight and
then poured into a separatory funnel containing EtOAc and sat. aq.
NaHCO3. The aqueous layer was extracted with EtOAc (3 x). The combined
organic extracts were washed with 1 N HCl, 10% LiCl and sat. NaCl and
then dried over Na2SO4, filtered and concentrated in vacuo. Following the
general procedure for amide coupling, crude 53 (818 mg, 1.06 mmol) and
(S)-2-((tertbutoxycarbonyl)( methyl)amino)propanoic acid (44, 450 mg,
2.22 mmol) were converted to 54 (0.99 g, 82%) after purification using
flash column chromatography (gradient from 0 to 80% EtOAc/CH2Cl2). 1H NMR
(400 MHz, CDCl3, mixture of amide rotamers) δ 7.43-7.37 (m, 1H), 7.30 (br
s, 1H), 7.22 (d, J = 7.0 Hz, 2H), 7.17-7.10 (m, 4H), 7.10-6.97 (m, 3H),
6.82 (d, J = 8.6 Hz, 1H), 5.24-5.14 (m, 2H), 5.08-4.94 (m, 2H), 4.77-4.52
(m, 4H), 4.41-4.26 (m, 2H), 3.48-3.26 (m, 3H), 3.08-2.97 (m, 1H), 2.79
(br s, 6H), 2.77-2.72 (m, 2H), 2.69-2.58 (m, 1H), 2.50 (dt, J = 12.7, 6.4
Hz, 1H), 2.07-1.99 (m, 3H), 1.96-1.67 (m, 6H), 1.60 (s, 9H), 1.49 (s,
9H), 1.33 (d, J = 7.3 Hz, 3H), 1.29 (d, J = 7.0 Hz, 3H), 1.02 (s, 9H),
0.90 (s, 9H); MS(ESI+) m/z 1146.2 (M + H)+.
