$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Synthesis of 7-18 and 22-24. The fatty acids
(C12, C12 diacid monoester, C18, and C18 monoester, 4 equiv) were coupled
to the linker-dimer conjugates (4-6 and 20, 21) using HBTU (4 equiv,
0.5M) and DIEA (8 equiv) in dry DMF for the shorter-chain acids and dry
DCM/DMF (75:25) for the longer-chain acids. After the coupling was
complete, the FA-linked dimeric ligands were cleaved from the resin with
concomitant side chain deprotection using TFA/TiPS/H2O (90:5:5). The
methyl protection group of the monoprotected FAs was then removed by
stirring the cleaved products in 0.5 M LiOH in H2O/ ACN 75/25 (100 mL)
for 30 min followed by acidification with TFA. The resulting mixture was
lyophilized. Purification of the crude FAlinked dimeric ligands was
conducted by dissolving the ligand in the smallest possible volume of
100% DMSO (<10 mL) before purification by large-scale C18 RP-HPLC. The
semipure fractions (50-90% purity) were subsequently lyophilized,
redissolved in a small volume of DMSO, diluted to 10 mL with ACN/H2O/TFA
(70/30/ 0.1), and purified by C4 RP-HPLC to give the pure compounds in
>95% purity (Scheme 1). Characterization of 7-18 and 22-24 is shown in
Table S1. Ligand: 15; Yield: 2.4 mg (3.9%); purity: 95%. formula:
C77H136N12O26; Calc. Mass [M+H+]: 1645.97; Obs. Mass LC-MS (m/z): 823.6,
1646.1; Obs. Mass MALDI-TOF (m/z): 1668.65 (+Na+).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM solid-supported reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Design, Synthesis, and Characterization of Fatty Acid Derivatives of a
Dimeric Peptide-Based Postsynaptic Density-95 (PSD-95) Inhibitor
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Nissen, Klaus B.; Andersen, Julie J.; Haugaard-Kedstrom, Linda M.; Bach,
Anders; Stroemgaard, Kristian
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Medicinal Chemistry (2015), 58(3), 1575-1580

